  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2021-03-22T08:59:49.058Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "A bug recently came up that is rather annoying, especially with avatars that have togglable objects, due to each mesh sampling light from a different location, or avatars with separate clothing meshes, such as sleeves which can disappear at certain angles locally.  Locally the bounds and centre for meshes is restored to their default values, ignoring any changes in unity editor.  With thorough testing, confirmed this to be a local problem only, and even with the attempt to force it with animating, it is not overridden.\n\nedit: animating update offscreen to 0 and animating bounds/centre to my desired values counteracts this issue, indicating update offscreen is turned on for meshes locally.",
